        {
          "published_at": "2026-10-20T15:47:58.456Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/steipete/status/2112571535731106013",
          "topic": "Agent-assisted Rust TypeScript compiler adoption",
          "text": "Moved to tsrs over the weekend. Drop-in replacement. Around 5x faster for OC.\n\nKind of amazing that it took Microsoft a team and two years to rewrite the TS compiler in go, and now you can just let an agent rip and get sth significantly better within weeks.",
          "quote_tweet": {
            "url": "https://x.com/voidzerodev/status/2112531443591020965",
            "published_at": "2026-10-20T13:08:38.993Z",
            "author": {
              "name": "VoidZero",
              "handle": "voidzerodev"
            },
            "text": "Introducing tsrs: a Rust port of the TypeScript compiler 🦀\n\nWe are not forking TypeScript!\n\n◆ In close collaborating with the TypeScript team\n◆ Up to 8x faster than TS 7.0 & ~70% less memory\n◆ Runs in WASM, so it works in your browser & on Workers\n◆ Soon part of the Oxc toolchain\n\nnpx tsrs\n\nblog.cloudflare.com/typescript-rus…",
